# GitHub Actions Secrets Configuration
# 
# This project uses GitHub Actions for secret management.
# Environment variables are passed directly to the application at runtime.
# 
# To configure secrets:
# 1. Go to GitHub repository Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions
# 2. Click "New repository secret"
# 3. Add your secrets (examples below)
# 4. GitHub Actions workflows will inject them as environment variables
#
# Available environment variables (these are optional, defaults shown):
# 
# PORT=3000              (default: 3000)
# NODE_ENV=production    (default: development)
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1   (default: us-east-1)
# LOG_LEVEL=info         (default: info)
#
# Example: If you add a GitHub secret called "DATABASE_URL",
# it will be available as process.env.DATABASE_URL in your application.
#
# See .github/workflows/*.yml for how secrets are passed to the application.
